\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {GSS 2024 left/right reference poles.} The 27 listed item--response assignments are the complete nonmissing coordinates of the two pole states used to compute $I_\Phi $. All other survey variables are unspecified. Topics paraphrase item wording; categorical responses match the simulation definitions. The poles yield $I_\Phi =-1$ and $+1$.}}{3}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:poles}{{I}{3}{\textbf {GSS 2024 left/right reference poles.} The 27 listed item--response assignments are the complete nonmissing coordinates of the two pole states used to compute $I_\Phi $. All other survey variables are unspecified. Topics paraphrase item wording; categorical responses match the simulation definitions. The poles yield $I_\Phi =-1$ and $+1$}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after 20{} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from 40{} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. These are native conditional-model trajectories, not observed human persuasion.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch_adaptive}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. These are native conditional-model trajectories, not observed human persuasion}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. These are native conditional-model trajectories, not observed human persuasion}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:persona-endpoints}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. These are native conditional-model trajectories, not observed human persuasion}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:native-trajectories}{{1}{3}{\textbf {DTAG digital-twin circuit and adaptive native GSS 2024 results.} (a) A semantic LLM interface maps and verbalizes categorical survey questions, while the conditional LSM inside the digital twin predicts unasked responses; a myopic greedy circuit selects the next question using expected one-step pole-relative displacement and updates the anchored state with a model draw. (b) Mean displacement after \DTAGSteps {} questions across six synthetic personas; large markers and horizontal whiskers show 95\% bootstrap uncertainty. (c) Six aligned trajectories from \DTAGReps {} repetitions per persona and policy; shading denotes pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals. Right = dark red, left = dark blue, neutral = dashed gray, random = black. These are native conditional-model trajectories, not observed human persuasion}{figure.1}{}}
